    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the tip. i was leaning toward blood meal too. do you think the compost i just added is gonna interfere with the blood meal absorbing, or should they work okay together? also just curious if there's anything else in the soil i should be looking at to make sure the nitrogen actually reaches the roots effectively.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Compost and blood meal should generally work together well, as long as you don't pile them on top of each other like a giant mound of sludge. Think of the compost as the slow-release, foundational layer, and the blood meal as a more immediate, though still organic, boost. If you're worried about absorption, you could lightly incorporate the blood meal into the top few inches of soil rather than just broadcasting it on top. You might also want to consider a light watering after application to help dissolve and move the nutrients around, which is key for root uptake.",
      "source": "target",
